  "id": "Compound::DB06702 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Fesoterodine, a muscarinic acetylcholine receptor antagonist, is shown to bind to Chrm5, which is involved in the activation of G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptors. This binding leads to the participation of Chrm5 in various receptor activities, including those related to muscarinic receptors and G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity. These pathways ultimately result in the participation of Chrm3, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Fesoterodine influences the function of muscarinic receptors, particularly Chrm3. The evidence from the three paths indicates a consistent relationship between Fesoterodine and Chrm3 through the intermediary of Chrm5, highlighting a mechanistic link that is supported by the observed interactions. The integration of these pathways suggests that Fesoterodine may modulate the activity of Chrm3 via muscarinic receptor pathways, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this mechanism definitively.",
